  "prefLabel": "We 101.18 Grout",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 101.18 “Grout” means a fluid mixture of cement and water, bentonite and water or both, possibly with additives, of a consistency which can be forced through a pipe and which is designed to provide a seal.\n\nSource. #6448, eff 1-29-97; ss by #7306, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9177, eff 6-13-08 (from We 101.15); renumbered by #12075 (formerly We 101.16)",
